From: aditya kale <252700881+kaleaditya28897-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:40:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] malloc: a configuration may start with no dynamic mmap
 threshold

MALLOC_NO_DYN_THRESHOLD (default 0) gives mp_.no_dyn_threshold its
initial value, as mallopt (M_MMAP_THRESHOLD) or the mmap_threshold
tunable would set it, without initialising malloc before the tunables
are read.  Joist, Phase 5 exit: the main arena's break is a region of
at most 8 MiB, its frames taken as it grows; with the threshold raised
by each free of an mmap'd block, large blocks went to the main arena,
past the break into mmap'd pieces it never gives back
(stdlib/tst-qsort2 reached its 32 MiB).  sysdeps/joist/Makefile sets it
to 1 for malloc.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 malloc/malloc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/malloc/malloc.c b/malloc/malloc.c
--- a/malloc/malloc.c
+++ b/malloc/malloc.c
@@ -1818,9 +1818,14 @@
 
 /* There is only one instance of the malloc parameters.  */
 
+#ifndef MALLOC_NO_DYN_THRESHOLD
+# define MALLOC_NO_DYN_THRESHOLD 0
+#endif
+
 static struct malloc_par mp_ =
 {
   .top_pad = DEFAULT_TOP_PAD,
+  .no_dyn_threshold = MALLOC_NO_DYN_THRESHOLD,
   .n_mmaps_max = DEFAULT_MMAP_MAX,
   .mmap_threshold = DEFAULT_MMAP_THRESHOLD,
   .trim_threshold = DEFAULT_TRIM_THRESHOLD,
-- 
2.43
